le A, open file B, ",[36,1549,1550],{"class":194},"`defer b.Close()`",[36,1552,58],{"class":50},[36,1554,1555],{"class":194},"`defer a.Close()`",[36,1557,1558],{"class":50},". LIFO ensures B (opened last) is closed first, matching resource lifetimes.\n",[36,1560,1561,1563,1565,1568,1570,1573,1575,1578,1580,1583,1586,1589,1592,1595,1597,1600,1603],{"class":38,"line":249},[36,1562,260],{"class":42},[36,1564,1360],{"class":42},[36,1566,1567],{"class":50},"Debug",[36,1569,1366],{"class":42},[36,1571,1572],{"class":50},": ",[36,1574,1027],{"class":194},[36,1576,1577],{"class":50}," arguments are evaluated at ",[36,1579,321],{"class":42},[36,1581,1582],{"class":50}," time, not at execution time — ",[36,1584,1585],{"class":194},"`defer fmt.Println(i)`",[36,1587,1588],{"class":50}," prints the value of ",[36,1590,1591],{"class":194},"`i`",[36,1593,1594],{"class":50}," when ",[36,1596,1027],{"class":194},[36,1598,1599],{"class":50}," was called, not when it runs. To capture the later value, use a closure: ",[36,1601,1602],{"class":194},"`defer func() { fmt.Println(i) }()`",[36,1604,1412],{"class":50},[36,1606,1607],{"class":38,"line":254},[36,1608,101],{"emptyLinePlaceholder":100},[36,1610,1611,1614,1616],{"class":38,"line":274},[36,1612,1613],{"class":50},"## ⚠️ Edge Cases ",[36,1615,1346],{"class":42},[36,1617,1618],{"class":50}," Gotchas\n",[36,1620,1621],{"class":38,"line":280},[36,1622,101],{"emptyLinePlaceholder":100},[36,1624,1625,1627,1629,1631,1634,1636,1638,1641],{"class":38,"line":286},[36,1626,260],{"class":42},[36,1628,1360],{"class":42},[36,1630,1027],{"class":194},[36,1632,1633],{"class":50}," in a loop",[36,1635,1366],{"class":42},[36,1637,1572],{"class":50},[36,1639,1640],{"class":194},"`for ... { defer f.Close() }`",[36,1642,1643],{"class":50}," accumulates deferred calls until the function returns — resources pile up. Close inside the loop, or refactor the loop body into a function.\n",[36,1645,1646,1648,1650,1652,1655,1657,1660,1663,1666,1668,1671,1673,1675,1677,1680,1683,1685,1688,1690,1693,1695,1697,1700,1702,1704,1707,1709],{"class":38,"line":292},[36,1647,260],{"class":42},[36,1649,1360],{"class":42},[36,1651,1027],{"class":194},[36,1653,1654],{"class":50}," and loops ",[36,1656,85],{"class":42},[36,1658,1659],{"class":50}," closures (",[36,1661,1662],{"class":175},"1.22",[36,1664,1665],{"class":50}," fix)",[36,1667,1366],{"class":42},[36,1669,1670],{"class":50},": pre",[36,1672,260],{"class":42},[36,1674,1662],{"class":175},[36,1676,58],{"class":50},[36,1678,1679],{"class":194},"`for i := 0; ... { defer func() { fmt.Println(i) }() }`",[36,1681,1682],{"class":50}," printed the ",[36,1684,678],{"class":42},[36,1686,1687],{"class":50},"final",[36,1689,678],{"class":42},[36,1691,1692],{"class":50}," value of ",[36,1694,1591],{"class":194},[36,1696,1030],{"class":42},[36,1698,1699],{"class":50}," all iterations (loop variable captured by reference). Go ",[36,1701,1662],{"class":175},[36,1703,85],{"class":42},[36,1705,1706],{"class":50}," makes each iteration",[36,1708,1487],{"class":194},[36,1710,1711],{"class":1490},"s loop variable distinct, fixing this. On older Go, pass `i` as an argument: `defer func(i int) { ... }(i)`.\n",[36,1713,1714],{"class":38,"line":301},[36,1715,1716],{"class":1490},"- **Naked returns in long functions**: `return` (no values) in a 100-line function with named returns is opaque — readers must scan for where the named returns were set. Use naked returns only in short functions.\n",[36,1718,1719],{"class":38,"line":307},[36,1720,1721],{"class":1490},"- **`defer` has a small overhead**: each `defer` has a tiny cost (function call + stack bookkeeping). In hot paths (millions of iterations), it can matter — Go 1.14+ optimized the common case (open-coded defer) to near-zero, but `defer` in a loop still adds up.\n",[36,1723,1724,1727,1729,1732,1735,1737,1740,1743,1745,1748,1751],{"class":38,"line":1097},[36,1725,1726],{"class":1490},"- **Multiple returns must be fully received or discarded**: `f, err := os.Open(...)` — you must use both (or `_`). You can",[36,1728,1487],{"class":194},[36,1730,1731],{"class":50},"t receive only one of a multi",[36,1733,1734],{"class":42},"-return",[36,1736,1572],{"class":50},[36,1738,1739],{"class":194},"`f := os.Open(...)`",[36,1741,1742],{"class":50}," is an ",[36,1744,891],{"class":42},[36,1746,1747],{"class":50},". Use ",[36,1749,1750],{"class":194},"`f, _ := ...`",[36,1752,1753],{"class":50}," to discard explicitly.\n",[36,1755,1757,1759,1761,1764,1767,1769,1771,1774,1777,1780,1783,1786,1789,1792,1795,1797],{"class":38,"line":1756},25,[36,1758,260],{"class":42},[36,1760,1360],{"class":42},[36,1762,1763],{"class":194},"`...`",[36,1765,1766],{"class":50}," spread requires a slice, not a single value",[36,1768,1366],{"class":42},[36,1770,1572],{"class":50},[36,1772,1773],{"class":194},"`sum(nums...)`",[36,1775,1776],{"class":50}," where ",[36,1778,1779],{"class":194},"`nums`",[36,1781,1782],{"class":50}," is ",[36,1784,1785],{"class":194},"`[]int`",[36,1787,1788],{"class":50}," works; ",[36,1790,1791],{"class":194},"`sum(5...)`",[36,1793,1794],{"class":50}," doesn",[36,1796,1487],{"class":194},[36,1798,1799],{"class":1490},"t. The `...` is the spread operator for variadic calls.\n",[36,1801,1803,1806,1808,1811,1813],{"class":38,"line":1802},26,[36,1804,1805],{"class":1490},"- **Function types are distinct**: `func(int) int` and `func(int64) int` are different types — you can",[36,1807,1487],{"class":194},[36,1809,1810],{"class":50},"t assign one to the other. This matches Go",[36,1812,1487],{"class":194},[36,1814,1815],{"class":1490},"s no-implicit-conversion rule.\n",[36,1817,1819],{"class":38,"line":1818},27,[36,1820,1821],{"class":1490},"- **Closures capture by reference**: `for i := 0; i \u003C 3; i++ { go func() { fmt.Println(i) }() }` (pre-1.22) prints \"3 3 3\" — all goroutines see the final `i`. Pass `i` as an argument: `go func(i int) { ... }(i)`.\n",[36,1823,1825,1828,1830,1833,1836,1838,1840,1843,1846,1848],{"class":38,"line":1824},28,[36,1826,1827],{"class":1490},"- **`defer` doesn",[36,1829,1487],{"class":194},[36,1831,1832],{"class":50},"t run on ",[36,1834,1835],{"class":194},"`os.Exit`",[36,1837,1366],{"class":42},[36,1839,1572],{"class":50},[36,1841,1842],{"class":194},"`os.Exit(n)`",[36,1844,1845],{"class":50}," terminates immediately without running deferred functions. Don",[36,1847,1487],{"class":194},[36,1849,1850],{"class":1490},"t call `os.Exit` inside a function with cleanup `defer`s — return an error and let `main` exit.\n",[36,1852,1854],{"class":38,"line":1853},29,[36,1855,101],{"emptyLinePlaceholder":100},[36,1857,1859],{"class":38,"line":1858},30,[36,1860,1861],{"class":1490},"## 🧠 Spot the Bug\n",[36,1863,1865],{"class":38,"line":1864},31,[36,1866,101],{"emptyLinePlaceholder":100},[36,1868,1870],{"class":38,"line":1869},32,[36,1871,1872],{"class":1490},"A developer opens files in a loop to process them, but runs out of file descriptors:\n",[36,1874,1876],{"class":38,"line":1875},33,[36,1877,101],{"emptyLinePlaceholder":100},[36,1879,1881],{"class":38,"line":1880},34,[36,1882,1883],{"class":1490},"::code-wrapper{language=\"go\"}\n",[36,1885,1887],{"class":38,"line":1886},35,[36,1888,277],{"class":1490},[36,1890,1892],{"class":38,"line":1891},36,[36,1893,1894],{"class":1490},"func processFiles(paths []string) error {\n",[36,1896,1898],{"class":38,"line":1897},37,[36,1899,1900],{"class":1490},"    for _, p := range paths {\n",[36,1902,1904],{"class":38,"line":1903},38,[36,1905,1906],{"class":1490},"        f, err := os.Open(p)\n",[36,1908,1910],{"class":38,"line":1909},39,[36,1911,1912],{"class":1490},"        if err != nil {\n",[36,1914,1916],{"class":38,"line":1915},40,[36,1917,1918],{"class":1490},"            return err\n",[36,1920,1922],{"class":38,"line":1921},41,[36,1923,1924],{"class":1490},"        }\n",[36,1926,1928],{"class":38,"line":1927},42,[36,1929,1930],{"class":1490},"        defer f.Close()   \u002F\u002F ❌ deferred until processFiles returns\n",[36,1932,1934],{"class":38,"line":1933},43,[36,1935,1936],{"class":1490},"        \u002F\u002F process f...\n",[36,1938,1940],{"class":38,"line":1939},44,[36,1941,396],{"class":1490},[36,1943,1945],{"class":38,"line":1944},45,[36,1946,1947],{"class":1490},"    return nil\n",[36,1949,1951],{"class":38,"line":1950},46,[36,1952,94],{"class":1490},[14,1954,312],{},[14,1956,1957],{},"What's wrong?",[1959,1960,1961,1965,1979,1988,1994,2167,2177],"details",{},[1962,1963,1964],"summary",{},"Answer",[14,1966,1967,1970,1971,1974,1975,1978],{},[33,1968,1969],{},"defer f.Close()"," doesn't run until ",[33,1972,1973],{},"processFiles"," returns — so all files stay open for the duration of the loop. With many files, you exhaust file descriptors (",[33,1976,1977],{},"EMFILE: too many open files",").",[14,1980,1981,1983,1984,1987],{},[33,1982,321],{}," is function-scoped, not block-scoped. In a loop, deferred calls accumulate; they only run when the enclosing ",[1107,1985,1986],{},"function"," returns, not at the end of each iteration.",[14,1989,1990,1991,1993],{},"The fix — extract the loop body into a function so each ",[33,1992,321],{}," runs per iteration:",[27,1995,1997],{"className":29,"code":1996,"language":25,"meta":31,"style":31},"func processFiles(paths []string) error {\n    for _, p := range paths {\n        if err := processFile(p); err != nil {\n            return err\n        }\n    }\n    return nil\n}\n\nfunc processFile(path string) error {\n    f, err := os.Open(path)\n    if err != nil {\n        return err\n    }\n    defer f.Close()   \u002F\u002F runs when processFile returns — per file\n    \u002F\u002F process f...\n    return nil\n}\n",[33,1998,1999,2022,2036,2057,2064,2068,2072,2079,2083,2087,2105,2117,2129,2135,2139,2152,2157,2163],{"__ignoreMap":31},[36,2000,2001,2003,2006,2008,2011,2013,2016,2018,2020],{"class":38,"line":39},[36,2002,43],{"class":42},[36,2004,2005],{"class":46}," processFiles",[36,2007,51],{"class":50},[36,2009,2010],{"class":